      "collapsed": true,
      "panels": [
        {
          "id": 8,
          "type": "stat",
          "title": "Writes / sec → evtx",
          "description": "Records per second reaching the configured output — the .evtx file on this deployment. cee_events_written_total counts what the writer accepted, so this is the rate the audit file actually grows at.\n\nIt should track Events received exactly; a persistent gap is backlog and Queue depth says how much. Deliveries, not distinct filesystem operations: nothing here deduplicates, and CEE on this estate redelivers one event from 2026-08-14 on every heartbeat. See Events per heartbeat. A replayed event is written again on every delivery, so this is also the rate duplicate records accumulate.",
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 4,
            "w": 4,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 15
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cee-prometheus"
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "expr": "sum(rate(cee_events_written_total[5m]))",
              "refId": "A",
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "cee-prometheus"
              },
              "legendFormat": ""
            }
          ],
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "wps",
              "decimals": 3,
              "thresholds": {
                "mode": "absolute",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "color": "text",
                    "value": null
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            "overrides": []
          },
          "options": {
            "reduceOptions": {
              "calcs": [
                "lastNotNull"
              ],
              "fields": "",
              "values": false
            },
            "textMode": "auto",
            "graphMode": "area",
            "justifyMode": "auto",
            "colorMode": "none"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "type": "stat",
          "title": "Events in range",
          "description": "Absolute count of events received over the dashboard's selected time range — the number behind the rate. Over a 65-second window against this estate it reads 6, matching the six CheckEventRequest batches counted on the wire in that span.\n\nFollows the time picker, so widening the range widens the count. Deliveries, not distinct filesystem operations: nothing here deduplicates, and CEE on this estate redelivers one event from 2026-08-14 on every heartbeat. See Events per heartbeat.\n\nAn estimate, not a count. increase() extrapolates to the window edges and sums across counter resets, so it can exceed the number of events actually seen — measured here reporting 1097 over an hour against a raw counter of 984, spanning exporter restarts.",
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 4,
            "w": 4,
            "x": 4,
            "y": 15
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cee-prometheus"
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "expr": "sum(increase(cee_events_received_total[$__range]))",
              "refId": "A",
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "cee-prometheus"
              },
              "legendFormat": ""
            }
          ],
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "short",
              "decimals": 1,
              "thresholds": {
                "mode": "absolute",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "color": "text",
                    "value": null
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            "overrides": []
          },
          "options": {
            "reduceOptions": {
              "calcs": [
                "lastNotNull"
              ],
              "fields": "",
              "values": false
            },
            "textMode": "auto",
            "graphMode": "area",
            "justifyMode": "auto",
            "colorMode": "none"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "type": "stat",
          "title": "Writes in range",
          "description": "Records written to the .evtx over the selected range. Equal to Events in range on a healthy pipeline; short of it means the difference is still queued, dropped or truncated.\n\nAn estimate, not a count. increase() extrapolates to the window edges and sums across counter resets, so it can exceed the number of events actually seen — measured here reporting 1097 over an hour against a raw counter of 984, spanning exporter restarts.",
          "gridPos": {
