        {
          "id": 12,
          "type": "stat",
          "title": "Deliveries per heartbeat",
          "description": "Event deliveries divided by heartbeats across all publishers — a replay detector derived from counters that already existed.\n\nRead the STEADINESS, not the level. The level is arbitrary: heartbeats are summed over every publisher while events arrive from CEE alone, so this estate sits at 0.20 (0.1 events/s against 0.5 heartbeats/s from six publishers), not at 1.00. What matters is that it does not move.\n\nA value that holds exactly constant means deliveries are clocked by the connection rather than produced by filesystem activity — CEE redelivering an event it cannot retire. Real traffic is bursty and this value moves. Zero means nothing is being delivered at all.\n\nA signature, not a proof. Confirm on the wire, where a replay shows byte-identical timeStamp, path and inode on every delivery — as it does here, for an event dated 2026-08-14.",
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 4,
            "w": 4,
            "x": 16,
            "y": 15
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cee-prometheus"
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "expr": "sum(rate(cee_events_received_total[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(cee_cepa_heartbeats_total[5m])), 0.0001)",
              "refId": "A",
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "cee-prometheus"
              },
              "legendFormat": ""
            }
          ],
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "short",
              "decimals": 2,
              "thresholds": {
                "mode": "absolute",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "color": "text",
                    "value": null
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            "overrides": []
          },
          "options": {
            "reduceOptions": {
              "calcs": [
                "lastNotNull"
              ],
              "fields": "",
              "values": false
            },
            "textMode": "auto",
            "graphMode": "area",
            "justifyMode": "auto",
            "colorMode": "none"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Diagnostics",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15
      },
      "collapsed": true,
      "panels": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "type": "bargauge",
          "title": "Publisher silence",
          "description": "Seconds since each publisher last said anything. The question is which one has gone quiet, so the publishers are ranked against a common scale and a threshold rather than shown as six separate numbers you have to compare by eye.\n\nThresholds are set against CEE's HeartBeatIntervalSecs, default 10: amber past 30s, red past 60s — three and six intervals. A publisher in red has missed several heartbeats and is the one to chase.\n\nScrape interval inflates this. The gauge cannot be fresher than the last scrape, so with Prometheus at 15s a perfectly healthy 10s heartbeat reads anywhere from 0 to about 25s, and a test stack scraping at 30s reads up to 40s. Judge the thresholds, not small values — and do not set a scrape interval longer than the heartbeat you are trying to observe.",
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 12,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 20
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "expr": "time() - cee_cepa_last_request_unix_seconds{remote=~\"$publisher\"}",
              "legendFormat": "{{remote}}",
              "refId": "A",
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "cee-prometheus"
              }
            }
          ],
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "s",
              "decimals": 0,
              "min": 0,
              "thresholds": {
                "mode": "absolute",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "color": "green",
                    "value": null
                  },
                  {
                    "color": "orange",
                    "value": 30
                  },
                  {
                    "color": "red",
                    "value": 60
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            "overrides": []
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cee-prometheus"
          },
          "options": {
            "displayMode": "gradient",
            "orientation": "horizontal",
            "showUnfilled": true,
            "valueMode": "color",
            "reduceOptions": {
              "calcs": [
                "lastNotNull"
              ],
              "fields": "",
              "values": false
            },
            "minVizWidth": 8,
            "minVizHeight": 16
          }
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "type": "timeseries",
          "title": "Handshakes per publisher",
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 12,
            "x": 12,
            "y": 20
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "expr": "rate(cee_cepa_registrations_total{remote=~\"$publisher\"}[5m])",
              "legendFormat": "{{remote}} register",
              "refId": "A",
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "cee-prometheus"
              }
            },
            {
              "expr": "rate(cee_cepa_heartbeats_total{remote=~\"$publisher\"}[5m])",
              "legendFormat": "{{remote}} heartbeat",
              "refId": "B",
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "cee-prometheus"
              }
            }
          ],
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "reqps",
              "custom": {
                "lineWidth": 2,
                "fillOpacity": 0,
                "showPoints": "never",
                "axisSoftMin": 0
              }
            },
            "overrides": [
              {
                "matcher": {
                  "id": "byRegexp",
                  "options": ".*heartbeat$"
                },
                "properties": [
                  {
                    "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                    "value": {
                      "fill": "dash",
                      "dash": [
                        10,
                        6
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cee-prometheus"
          },
          "description": "Registrations and heartbeats are separate series because they mean different things. Only a CEE server sends RegisterRequest; arrays publishing directly (PowerStore Data Movers, OneFS nodes) only ever heartbeat, so zero registrations against a healthy heartbeat rate is normal for them. Until v5.4.2 both were counted as registrations, so this panel showed a registration rate for publishers that had never registered.",
          "options": {
            "legend": {
              "displayMode": "list",
              "placement": "bottom",
              "showLegend": true
            },
            "tooltip": {
              "mode": "multi",
              "sort": "desc"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "type": "stat",
          "title": "Publishers reporting",
          "description": "Distinct CEPA publishers seen. A publisher is whatever opened the connection — a CEE server, or an array publishing directly — which is not the same as where the event happened. A NAS whose events a CEE server relays never appears here at all; look for it in Events by NAS server. A drop means someone stopped talking; Publisher silence says who.",
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 12,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 28
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cee-prometheus"
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "expr": "count(cee_cepa_last_request_unix_seconds{remote=~\"$publisher\"})",
              "refId": "A",
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "cee-prometheus"
              },
              "legendFormat": ""
            }
          ],
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "short",
              "thresholds": {
                "mode": "absolute",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "color": "text",
                    "value": null
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            "overrides": []
          },
          "options": {
            "reduceOptions": {
              "calcs": [
                "lastNotNull"
              ],
              "fields": "",
              "values": false
            },
            "textMode": "auto",
            "graphMode": "area",
            "justifyMode": "auto",
            "colorMode": "none"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "type": "timeseries",
          "title": "Event throughput",
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 12,
            "x": 12,
            "y": 28
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "expr": "rate(cee_events_received_total[5m])",
              "legendFormat": "{{instance}} received",
              "refId": "A",
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "cee-prometheus"
              }
            },
            {
              "expr": "rate(cee_events_written_total[5m])",
              "legendFormat": "{{instance}} written",
              "refId": "B",
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "cee-prometheus"
              }
            },
            {
              "expr": "rate(cee_events_dropped_total[5m])",
              "legendFormat": "{{instance}} dropped",
              "refId": "C",
              "datasource": {
                "type": "prometheus",
                "uid": "cee-prometheus"
              }
            }
          ],
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "eps",
              "custom": {
                "lineWidth": 2,
                "fillOpacity": 0,
                "showPoints": "never",
                "axisSoftMin": 0
              }
            },
            "overrides": [
              {
                "matcher": {
                  "id": "byRegexp",
                  "options": ".*written$"
                },
                "properties": [
                  {
                    "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                    "value": {
                      "fill": "dash",
                      "dash": [
                        10,
                        6
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "matcher": {
                  "id": "byRegexp",
                  "options": ".*dropped$"
                },
                "properties": [
                  {
                    "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                    "value": {
                      "fill": "dash",
                      "dash": [
                        2,
                        4
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cee-prometheus"
          },
          "description": "Events per second, per exporter instance. received is what was parsed off the wire, written is what reached the output, dropped is what was lost — so received is the parse rate and received minus written is backlog.\n\nThe three series overlap exactly on a healthy pipeline: received and written carry identical values and one hides the other, which reads as a single line or as no line at all when it sits against the top of the axis. written and dropped are dashed so received stays visible beneath them, and the legend carries the numbers so the panel is readable even when the traces coincide.",
          "options": {
            "legend": {
              "displayMode": "table",
              "placement": "bottom",
              "showLegend": true,
              "calcs": [
                "lastNotNull",
                "max"
              ]
            },
            "tooltip": {
              "mode": "multi",
              "sort": "desc"
            }
          }
        },
