            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "type": "timeseries",
          "title": "Events by NAS server",
          "description": "Where the operation happened — the array's own name for itself, taken from the event rather than from the connection.\n\nThis is the question cee_cepa_* cannot answer. Those metrics label by publisher, which for a relayed event is the CEE server, so a NAS behind a CEE server appears here and nowhere else. A NAS that stops generating events while its CEE server keeps heartbeating is visible only on this panel.\n\nThe client address is deliberately not a label: it is every workstation that ever touched a share, and unbounded labels are how an exporter takes down its own Prometheus. Server is capped too — see cee_event_labels_dropped_total.",
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 8,
            "w": 12,
            "x": 12,
            "y": 44
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
